{
  "description": "Published MCP-server advisories whose bug is a tool argument reaching a file path, shell command or URL. Each case pins the advisory's fix commit; the vulnerable tree is its first parent. A case is caught when a dataflow finding (TNT-*, CF-* or structural boundary rule such as AGENT-TOOL-001, advisory CWE class) in a file the fix changed disappears at the fix commit, matched by rule, file and flagged line text. Pattern-only rules do not count. Checkouts are fetched into cache/ and not committed.",
